WEBVTT

NOTE editing-station-targets: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.430
Change one station's target, and
watch what it does to the suggestion.

V1a-1
00:00:13.626 --> 00:00:17.669
The table drills from course to
areas, then holes, then stations.

V1a-2
00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:21.066
Breadcrumbs at the top left
take you back up a level.

V1b-1
00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:26.698
If you already know where the
station is, click its pin on the map:

V1b-2
00:00:26.798 --> 00:00:30.096
the table drills straight to
its hole and scrolls to the row.

V2a-1
00:00:36.553 --> 00:00:40.923
The Target VWC field takes a
whole number between 0 and 50.

V2b-1
00:00:43.286 --> 00:00:47.046
Raising it increases the deficit
and therefore the suggestion;

V2b-2
00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.966
lowering it does the opposite.

V3a-1
00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.360
The Suggested column recalculates
against the new target.

V3b-1
00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:05.251
If it lands on the top value, Daily Max
Amount divided by Lynx Reference Amount

V3b-2
00:01:05.351 --> 00:01:09.853
times 100, the daily maximum is capping
it rather than the target deciding it.

V4a-1
00:01:17.613 --> 00:01:21.993
The % Adj. field is separate from
the target and accepts 0 to 900.

V4b-1
00:01:24.313 --> 00:01:27.592
Editing it queues the station
for push when the station is

V4b-2
00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:31.367
enabled and the new value differs
from the Current value in Lynx.

V4b-3
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.803
The Suggested value stays
visible beside it for comparison.
